WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.702
-Our next guest is a talented
singer and song writer

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.404
you know from
both his solo career

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:05.838
and work with One Direction.

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.073
His third solo album "The Show"

00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:10.409
will be out June and is
available for preorder now.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:13.078
He will also be a coach on the
new season of "The Voice,"

00:00:13.078 --> 00:00:15.481
which premieres March 6th
at 8:00 PM here on NBC.

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:16.682
Let's take a look.

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:19.152
-I nearly hit my button
on your first note.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.220
-Long enough for me to actually
figure it out before him.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.424
-Please, Kelly, come on.
Give me a chance.

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.826
You remind me so much of
my good friend Maren Morris.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.561
-Oh, my gosh.
-I've spent a lot of time

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.829
on the stage over the years
and become very, very, very

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:32.231
fond of country music,

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:34.833
and country always
leads into story telling,

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:36.703
and I tend to do that.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.706
Your voice, the control,
it was just unbelievable.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.141
I'm telling you,

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:42.909
we're going to do big things
together if you come with me.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.744
[ Cheers and applause ]
Please!

00:00:45.744 --> 00:00:48.214
-Please welcome to the show
Niall Horan, everybody!

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.217
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.217 --> 00:01:07.667 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.101
I'm so happy you're here,
my friend.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.103
-I'm happy to be here.
Huge fan of the show.

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:13.105
-We were very lucky to --

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:16.075
I was very lucky, I should say,
to work with you 10 years ago.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:19.245
You fellas were on the show,
and we did a sketch.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.348
I was on set for where Paul Rudd
was the number one.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:25.918
There we see Paul.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.918 --> 00:01:27.853
And I have spoken
for years about

00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:30.656
how you were
the nicest group of guys.

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.392
And, I mean, you were
fairly young at the time.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.093
Was that an exciting thing
to do?

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:37.096
-Oh, yeah.
It was crazy to be part of "SNL"

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:39.298
on a few occasions is so cool.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:43.269
But that particular weekend
Paul was hosting the show.

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.571
And the "Anchorman" crew
were there.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:47.006
-Yeah.
-They were promoting

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.341
"Anchorman 2."
-You got to sing with the --

00:01:49.341 --> 00:01:51.844
and this is two of the great
casts of all time.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:56.682
-"Anchorman"
being like, no joke,

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.117
my favorite movie of all time.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:02.722
And just be standing there
singing "Afternoon Delight"

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.857
with that bunch of lunatics

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:07.126
was pretty special.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.261
The other funny thing about
the sketch with Paul I remember

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.264
we had a great many extras

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:13.299
who also
were big One Direction fans.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.369
And it was the least we ever had
to give direction

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.938
to a group of young girls.
-"Applause. Applause. Applause."

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.640
They were already screaming.
-"When they walk out,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.074
like, lose your minds."

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:23.877
They were like,
"I think we can do that."

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.811
-Yeah, yeah.
"We can sort that out."

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.614
-This is very exciting.
You have a new single out.

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.215
-Yes, I do.
-You have a new album coming.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.416
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.118
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.920
-I think a lot of people --

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.122
you know, a lot of artists
reacted different ways

00:02:37.122 --> 00:02:38.691
to the pandemic
and what it put them through.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:40.693
-Yeah.
-Did you feel like you wanted to

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.295
start working on new music
right away?

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.696
Did you give yourself
a little time?

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:45.664
Because it's been a while since
you -- about three years?

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:46.666
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.468
No, I kind of --
I released an album

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:52.071
the day we were told we were
going into lockdown.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.872
Some would say
that was great timing.

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:55.341
[ Laughs ]

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.109
No, but it was
one of those things

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:59.579
where I release an album
and then that happened.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.313
And then the tour got cancelled.

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:02.781
So I was thinking like...

00:03:02.781 --> 00:03:04.917
I was kind of just angry
at the world, like we all were.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.619
-Yeah.
-So, then I was sitting around,

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.420
waiting for something to happen,

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.156
waiting for
the creative juices to flow.

00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.858
Took a while.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.360
And then once it came,
it kind of --

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:19.365
it opened the door for what is
now a finished product, record.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Very exciting.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:23.202
I wonder, do you --

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.470
I mean, obviously
you work on these songs

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.373
and a lot of
post production on the music

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.742
and finally get it to a place
where you're happy with it.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.344
And then it gets
released to the world.

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.347
Are you someone who --

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.248
Do you sort of anticipate
the reaction to it?

00:03:36.248 --> 00:03:38.651
Have you already moved on
to the next?

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:42.622
-No, I'm just always so nervous.
Like, it's the biggest cliche.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.757
When ever you work on something,

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.259
you just obviously want it
to do well.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:48.828
But we have no idea.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:50.363
Especially these days,
it's hard to know --

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.731
it's so competitive out there.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:54.634
But I've got --
as you can hear, I have --

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:58.438
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:01.874
I'm lucky enough to have
a strong, solid fan base.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:04.744
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.113
Having said that -- Having said
that, you still don't know.

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.515
So I'm just, like, after three
years of not releasing music,

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.584
there's that, like,
"Please do good."

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.886
-Yeah.
-But the reaction to

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:15.821
this single first of all
has been ridiculous,

00:04:15.821 --> 00:04:17.389
which makes me feel
a lot better about the record.

00:04:17.389 --> 00:04:18.824
-Well, there you go.
Very exciting.

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:20.325
And now this is really exciting,
'cause you talked about

00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:21.561
your last tour being cancelled.

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:23.329
You're going on the road
this summer

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.498
and you're doing
a great many festivals,

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.433
which is different that

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.969
sort of doing more
sort of conventional tour.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.837
Are you excited about
festival life?

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.839
-I think that is the main thing
I wanted to do

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:36.008
when I was finishing off
the record.

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:38.110
I said to everyone, like,
"I would love to just do

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.278
a summer of festivals,"

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:40.813
especially having spent
so much time away.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.516
It's good to get back
in front of people in that way.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.984
You know, I can go
all over the world,

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.286
and we're doing them
all over Europe and Japan

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:48.888
and a couple here in the states.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:52.058
And, like, it's just going to be
good to feel the love.

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:54.927
And I'm a huge festival goer
myself.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.662
I've been that drunk guy...

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:58.764
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.566
-...standing in my welly boots

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:03.569
in a field going,
"Who's that up there?

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.138
I like the sound of that."

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.373
So I want --
That's why I wanted to do it.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.608
I can get some new fans here,
Seth.

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.142
-Well, absolutely.

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:12.178
This speaks to the level
of difficulty of a festival.

00:05:12.178 --> 00:05:13.879
Because obviously, you know,
you have a group of people

00:05:13.879 --> 00:05:15.481
who are all music fans.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.116
-But, you know, specifically

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:19.418
they might be less there
to see you.

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.421
Like, they might be there
to see the person before you

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:23.689
or after you,
so you do have to win them over.

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:25.725
And I think
it's really impressive that

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:27.125
you want to take on
that challenge.

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:28.594
-Oh, for sure.
-You don't necessarily have to,

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.062
but I think that will be
so exciting.

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:32.331
-No, it's a great way
of getting, like, new people.

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:36.135
As you say, there's a solid
group there, but it's --

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:39.439
You know, I'd love to invite
more people into the world.

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:42.441
-Do you feel like you get to
meet and hang out

00:05:42.441 --> 00:05:43.943
with other bands
in the festival world?

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:47.847
Is that one of the up sides?
-Yeah, no. They're always good.

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.549
You meet people
that you have no idea

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.049
you had anything in common with,

00:05:51.049 --> 00:05:53.685
And before you know it's 2:00.
[ Laughs ]

00:05:53.685 --> 00:05:55.087
It's been a good night.
-Yeah?

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:56.489
[ Laughter ]
And Europe,

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:58.757
is it buses around Europe
when you're doing...?

00:05:58.757 --> 00:06:02.227
-Yeah. There's a lot of --
Because they're so far apart,

00:06:02.227 --> 00:06:04.430
other countries, you do have to
do a lot of flying.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.498
When we're in the states,
it's a lot of buses.

00:06:06.498 --> 00:06:08.367
-Do you enjoy -- Is bus life --

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.436
Because I feel there's something
a little romantic about it

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.638
maybe for the first three days.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.773
You're like,
you've seen "Spinal Tap" twice

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:18.010
and now you think
"Yeah, that's how it's done."

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.211
[ Laughs ]

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:22.749
Then it's like 105 degrees
in Houston, Texas.

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:25.784
First week of July,
and it's sweaty

00:06:25.784 --> 00:06:27.787
and you've woken up and
air-conditioning is broken.

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:30.756
It's just like, "Maybe not as
romantic as I thought."

00:06:30.756 --> 00:06:32.491
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.491 --> 00:06:35.394
-Um, one place that's very well
air-conditioned,

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:37.196
I've heard, is this studio
for "The Voice."

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:39.465
Congratulations on that gig.
-It's Baltic.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:44.337
-Is this --
How did this come to pass?

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:45.804
I'm assuming this is a situation

00:06:45.804 --> 00:06:48.340
where your phone just rang
one day and they reached out?

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:53.445
-Literally. Phone call from
the producers, Audrey, Kyra.

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:55.914
And they just said,
"Before you even say anything,

00:06:55.914 --> 00:06:57.183
just come in and meet us."

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:58.617
And they explained
how the show works

00:06:58.617 --> 00:07:00.753
and all that good stuff.

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.289
And I was like,
"Yeah, let's just give it a go.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.557
See what happens."

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.625
I've been on a show like that.
-Of course, yeah.

00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:09.195
-So, I un-- I do...

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:12.264
I understand --
I understand how it works.

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:14.199
But, yeah,
it was just a challenge,

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:15.601
something that
I wasn't expecting.

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.870
-Right.
-You know, a great time to do it

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.705
before I've got
a record coming out.

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:22.207
And you're going to be
sick of my faces.

00:07:22.207 --> 00:07:25.411
Or sick of my face.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.079
But, yeah, no,
it's been so fun.

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:30.816
We were very lucky with the crew
of coaches that I'm with.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:32.819
-Yeah.
-It could've been horrific.

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:34.887
You know, you're sitting there
every night pretending that

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:36.722
you like the person
you're sat next to.

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:40.292
I got very lucky
in Blake Shelton alone.

00:07:40.292 --> 00:07:41.293
-Yeah.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:42.928
-Now, I would imagine too

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:45.064
having gone through a show
like this, you must have --

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:46.732
because obviously
it looks very exciting

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:48.200
what we see on television.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.669
But you obviously are in this
situation you can have empathy

00:07:50.669 --> 00:07:52.037
with them
for what they're going through.

00:07:52.037 --> 00:07:54.807
Because I think we all maybe
forget how stressful it is

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:56.308
for an unknown artist to --

00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:57.676
especially in a room like that

00:07:57.676 --> 00:07:59.478
to be in front of
four very accomplished,

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:00.580
very famous singers.
-Yeah.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.515
-They must feel nice knowing

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:04.616
and being like, "Oh, I know
Niall has been on this side."

00:08:04.616 --> 00:08:06.452
-Whoo!
-I guess that's a part --

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:08.054
Ooh, That was a big one.

00:08:08.054 --> 00:08:09.121
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.556
No, it is -- It's good...

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:12.591
I think that's
how I got half of my team

00:08:12.591 --> 00:08:15.594
because they understand that
I've got that empathy with them.

00:08:15.594 --> 00:08:19.231
I was -- You know,
17-, 18-, 19-year-old people

00:08:19.231 --> 00:08:21.433
coming on here,
and I was that 16-year-old

00:08:21.433 --> 00:08:23.468
just kind of knowing
that person there

00:08:23.468 --> 00:08:25.237
has got my future
in their hands.

00:08:25.237 --> 00:08:27.940
And it's -- That's the hardest
thing about "The Voice."

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.542
It's like I have to make
in-game decisions

00:08:30.542 --> 00:08:33.045
over two singers that
are standing in front of me...

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:36.482
knowing that I have
their future in my hands.

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:39.351
And that's the part that I feel
like the empathy side of me.

00:08:39.351 --> 00:08:41.053
I hope I don't lose it,
because I would be heartless

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:43.322
if I did lose that.
-Well, I think if you want to

00:08:43.322 --> 00:08:45.457
know what it's like
to be without empathy,

00:08:45.457 --> 00:08:46.892
that feels like probably what
Blake Shelton does, right?

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:48.427
-Blake Shelton. There you go.

00:08:48.427 --> 00:08:52.798
After 12 years...
12 years and 23 seasons.

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:55.033
-Yeah.
-He's stone cold, that man.

00:08:55.033 --> 00:08:57.703
-He's stone cold. A man
who this is his last season.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:00.672
Obviously he's done a great
amount of success on the show.

00:09:00.672 --> 00:09:02.408
When ever he's here,

00:09:02.408 --> 00:09:05.210
he is not shy about
bragging about his success.

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:06.745
Has he been giving you
a hard time?

00:09:06.745 --> 00:09:08.347
Because he also seems
very good at that.

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:12.184
-That's all he does anywhere, to
everyone that will listen to him

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:14.286
or don't want to listen to him.
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:16.689
-He's just constantly
just nailing everyone.

00:09:16.689 --> 00:09:19.325
-He's a very charismatic
and affable bully.

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:22.795
-Yeah. [ Chuckles ] Correct.
That's exactly what he is.

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.329
But he's an absolute beauty.

00:09:24.329 --> 00:09:26.898
And, you know, he's going
to be missed around that show.

00:09:26.898 --> 00:09:30.202
Like, he is "The Voice" --
probably in his head, too.

00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:32.571
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:32.571 --> 00:09:35.775
-But he's so good to work with.

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:37.376
And, yeah, he'll be missed
around there for sure.

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.011
-I mean, yeah, I think one of
the reasons the show

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:41.714
is so exceptional
is the connection

00:09:41.714 --> 00:09:43.416
you guys all have together
and the chemistry.

00:09:43.416 --> 00:09:46.285
Do you feel like --
When he leaves,

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:48.687
do you feel like you'll have
a good Blake Shelton impression?

00:09:48.687 --> 00:09:50.355
Do you have one yet?
-[ As Blake ] I'm Blake Shelton.

00:09:50.355 --> 00:09:52.724
Uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.724 --> 00:09:54.360
This is my...

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.161
[ Normal voice ] I feel like a
politician every time I do it.

00:09:56.161 --> 00:09:59.097
[ Blake ] This is my last season
on "The Voice,"

00:09:59.097 --> 00:10:05.370
and I would love if you would be
on the last-ever Team Blake.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.539
[ Normal voice ] And he says
that to every single person

00:10:07.539 --> 00:10:10.943
who comes out --
win, lose or draw.

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:14.480
-I will tell you, I know you
said you felt like a politician,

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.781
but you said that
and looked at me,

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:17.149
I was like,
"I want to be on Team Blake."

00:10:17.149 --> 00:10:19.685
It totally worked.
It was very convincing.

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:21.921
-I need a catch phrase.
-You've got to work on it.

00:10:21.921 --> 00:10:23.989
Hey, man, what a pleasure
to have you here.

00:10:23.989 --> 00:10:25.157
I really can't thank you enough.

00:10:25.157 --> 00:10:27.226
And congratulations
on the new music.

00:10:27.226 --> 00:10:28.627
Niall Horan.

00:10:28.627 --> 00:10:30.095
His new album
"The Show"

00:10:30.095 --> 00:10:32.364
is available for preorder now,

00:10:32.364 --> 00:10:33.999
and "The Voice" premieres
March 6th at 8:00 PM

00:10:33.999 --> 00:10:35.200
right here on NBC.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.268
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

